          "Because Django's router handles other HTTP methods (or allows requests without strict verb gating unless explicitly enforced with `@require_http_methods`), an attacker could send a `PUT` or `OPTIONS` request. The authentication middleware looked at the request, saw it wasn't a standard POST that required its token check, and let it pass straight through to the internal view function!"
