          "**• Fail closed in security middleware:** Security middleware should never ask 'is this a method I should check?'. It must ask 'is this route explicitly public? If not, reject all unauthenticated requests regardless of verb.'",
          "**• Drop privileges early:** Running a web control server directly as `root` violates the principle of least privilege. Decoupling the user-facing web API (running as an unprivileged user) from a strictly audited local Unix socket daemon with restricted sudo capabilities would have contained this exploit completely."
        ]
